---
import FieldGuideLayout from '../../../components/FieldGuideLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<FieldGuideLayout
  title="Overlay system"
  description="180 dynamically loaded ARM9 overlays. Shared RAM slots, controller/body pattern, persistent rendering engines."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Field Guide', href: `${base}/field-guide/` },
    { label: 'How the Game Works', href: `${base}/field-guide/how-the-game-works/` },
    { label: 'Overlays' },
  ]}
>
  <h2>Overlay table</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Table at ROM offset <code>0x8DE00</code>, size <code>0x1680</code>.</li>
    <li>180 entries × 32 bytes per entry.</li>
    <li>Per entry: <code>ram_addr</code>, <code>ram_size</code>, <code>bss_size</code>, <code>file_id</code>, <code>flags</code>, <code>compressed_size</code>, <code>is_compressed</code>.</li>
    <li>Total decompressed overlay code: 1,927,488 bytes.</li>
    <li>Extracted via <code>ndspy.rom.NintendoDSRom.fromFile().loadArm9Overlays()</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Shared RAM slots</h2>
  <p>
    Many overlays map to the same RAM address — only one is resident at a
    time. The slot is selected by the game mode dispatcher in arm9.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>RAM address</th><th>Overlays sharing</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x02155A00</code></td><td>66</td><td>Game-mode body / controller overlays</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x021597A0</code></td><td>25</td><td>Body / renderer slot 1</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x0215C540</code></td><td>20</td><td>Body / renderer slot 2</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x021FB3C0</code></td><td>18</td><td>Body / renderer slot 3</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x021B6080</code></td><td>(ov156/157)</td><td>Body / renderer slot 4</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x021C3420</code></td><td>(ov158/159)</td><td>Body / renderer slot 5</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Persistent engines</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Overlay</th>
        <th>RAM</th>
        <th>Size</th>
        <th>BSS</th>
        <th>Role</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>ov137</code></td>
        <td><code>0x0216DA40</code></td>
        <td><code>0x20860</code></td>
        <td><code>0x27E0</code></td>
        <td>2D rendering engine (sprite API, OAM transfer, VBlank handler). Loaded persistently across most game modes.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>ov138</code></td>
        <td><code>0x0216DA40</code> (shares slot)</td>
        <td>varies</td>
        <td>—</td>
        <td>Tongari 3D map engine. Alternates with ov137 depending on game mode.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The VBlank handler at <code>0x02185BF8</code> in ov137 transfers shadow
    OAM to <code>0x07000000</code>/<code>0x07000400</code>. The ARM9 VBlank
    handler at <code>0x0207001C</code> handles the wider system (DMA timing,
    audio buffer, etc.).
  </p>

  <h2>Controller / body pattern</h2>
  <p>
    UI screens use a two-overlay pattern: a <strong>controller</strong>
    (state machine + asset loading) plus a <strong>body</strong> (per-screen
    sprite placement + interaction logic). The controller calls into the
    body at <code>FUN_xxxxxxxx</code> entry points; the body reads its
    sprite-placement table from <code>.rodata</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Known controller → body mappings</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Container</th><th>Controller</th><th>Body</th><th>Body init function</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>2d/buyitem.lzs</code></td><td>ov003</td><td>ov070</td><td><code>FUN_02159828</code> @ <code>0x02159828</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>2d/itemorderwnd.lzs</code></td><td>ov003 (shared)</td><td>ov070</td><td>same</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>2d/chest.lzs</code></td><td>ov013</td><td>TBD</td><td>—</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>2d/dustbox.lzs</code></td><td>ov013</td><td>TBD</td><td>—</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Per-overlay roles (excerpt)</h2>
  <p>Full table in <code>notes/phaseA_ghidra/overlay_role_final.json</code>. Highlights:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Overlay</th><th>RAM</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>ov003</code></td><td><code>0x02155A00</code></td><td>Buyitem controller (shop state machine)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ov010</code>, <code>ov041</code>, ...</td><td><code>0x02155A00</code></td><td>Game-mode controllers (66 share this slot)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ov070</code></td><td><code>0x021597A0</code></td><td>Buyitem body (renderer)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ov137</code></td><td><code>0x0216DA40</code></td><td>2D rendering engine (persistent)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ov138</code></td><td><code>0x0216DA40</code></td><td>3D map engine</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ov156/157</code></td><td><code>0x021B6080</code></td><td>Slot 4 bodies</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ov158/159</code></td><td><code>0x021C3420</code></td><td>Slot 5 bodies</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Nintendo DWC (wireless)</h2>
  <p>
    The VBlank handler in <code>ov137</code> is the game engine. The other
    VBlank handler that appears in some Konami DS builds is Nintendo DWC
    (wireless library) — not present here.
  </p>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>notes/phaseA_ghidra/DISCOVERIES.md</code> — overlay table + per-RAM-slot membership</li>
    <li><code>notes/phaseA_ghidra/overlay_role_final.json</code> — per-overlay role classification</li>
    <li><code>notes/phaseA_ghidra/BUYITEM_RECIPE_CRACKED.md</code> — controller/body pattern worked example</li>
  </ul>
</FieldGuideLayout>
